  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1249 PM MDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nWednesday will mostly be a transition day. Temperatures will remain \nhot across the region, similar to Mon-Tues, but with quickly \nincreasing moisture as a shortwave passes by our area aloft. \nConvection will become more widespread Wednesday afternoon, \nincreasing in coverage over all of our higher terrain. By evening \ninto Weds Night, another front will come down, spreading showers and \nthunderstorms to the eastern plains as well. These conditions will \nlast through Friday. Chances for heavy rainfall and flash flooding \nwill continue to increase, and burn scars will need to be monitored \nclosely alongside any other vulnerable areas.\n\nMoving into this weekend, forecast remains on track with previous \nmodel runs. Moisture appears to remain trapped under the high \npressure, recirculating each day and continuing chances for daily \nshowers and storms. Though most of the activity will still be over \nthe mountains, NBM does keep isolated to low-end scattered pops over \nI-25 and some of the adjacent plains as well.",
